{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Who is the man who has built a new house and has not dedicated it.</b> Like the expression of the dedication of the altar (חנכת המזבח). And the sage Rabbi Abraham, of blessed memory, wrote: since his heart and all his desire are to dedicate his house, and behold, his heart is in his house, not in the war — therefore he will flee and cause others to flee. And further it is written ולא חללו, from the word חלילים (flutes), for it was their custom to play flutes in the vineyards. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted ולא חללו — that he has not made it חולין (profane), for the planting requires redemption, and it is holy until he redeems it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:38.665077874Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}